Practical 10 : Date, Time and Calendar Module 

• 10.1 Print current date in different formats.

code :- 

from datetime import datetime
now = datetime.now()
print("Current Date:", now)
print("DD-MM-YYYY :", now.strftime("%d-%m-%Y"))
print("MM/DD/YYYY :", now.strftime("%m/%d/%Y"))
print("Day Month Year :", now.strftime("%d %B %Y"))
print("Day Name :", now.strftime("%A"))

• 10 .2Convert timestamp to datestamp.

code :- 

import time
timestamp = time.time()
print("Timestamp:", timestamp)
date = time.ctime(timestamp)
print("Datestamp:", date)

• 10.3 Compare two dates.

code :- 

from datetime import datetime
date1 = input("Enter First Date (DD-MM-YYYY): ")
date2 = input("Enter Second Date (DD-MM-YYYY): ")
d1 = datetime.strptime(date1, "%d-%m-%Y")
d2 = datetime.strptime(date2, "%d-%m-%Y")
if d1 > d2:
 print("First date is later.")
elif d1 < d2:
 print("Second date is later.")
else:
 print("Both dates are equal.")

•10.4 Display monthly/yearly calendar using calendar module.

code :-

import calendar
year = int(input("Enter Year: "))
month = int(input("Enter Month (1-12): "))
print("\nMonthly Calendar\n")
print(calendar.month(year, month))
print("\nYearly Calendar\n")
print(calendar.calendar(year))
